     held_one_custody(recorded=None), custody(1, CUSTODY_AT + 100, "active"), None),
    ("custody_store_fault_at_commit", "custody_acknowledgement",
     "The store fails at commit while first recording custody for local_seq 1. Rolled back: nothing is held, the artifact is neither applied nor refused, and the application-storage fault signal is raised.",
     held(), custody(1, CUSTODY_AT, "active"), "at_commit"),
    ("custody_conflict_refusal_record_unwritable", "custody_acknowledgement",
     "A restatement whose custody_at_ms conflicts with the held one. The refusal is decided, and then the store fails writing the record of that refusal. The refusal is still answered restatement_conflict, every held record is unchanged, and the failed write raises the signal.",
     held_one_custody(), custody(1, CUSTODY_AT + 100, "active"), "at_refusal_record"),
    ("custody_store_fault_reading_held_record", "custody_acknowledgement",
     "A restatement whose custody_at_ms conflicts with the held one, but the store fails reading the held custody record the decision needs. A read fault is a store fault even where the decision would have been a refusal: undecided, no rejection reason, nothing changes, and the signal is raised.",
     held_one_custody(), custody(1, CUSTODY_AT + 100, "active"), "at_read"),
    ("custody_conflict_leaves_fault_signal_raised", "custody_acknowledgement",
     "The fault signal is raised from an earlier fault. A refusal is not a successful application, so it stays raised.",
     held_one_custody(application_storage_fault=True), custody(1, CUSTODY_AT + 100, "active"), None),
    ("custody_agreeing_restatement_clears_fault_signal", "custody_acknowledgement",
     "The fault signal is raised from an earlier fault. An agreeing restatement is answered as applied, and its application completes, so the signal clears.",
     held_one_custody(application_storage_fault=True), custody(1, CUSTODY_AT, "active"), None),
    # receipts
    ("receipt_identical_repeat", "delivery_receipt",
